  "summary": "The code suffered from critical security vulnerabilities (SSRF), blocking I/O, and poor resource management. I have refactored the function to use an asynchronous approach with proper error handling, type hints, and strict URL scheme validation to improve both security and performance.",
  "fixed_code": "import json\nimport httpx\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\nfrom typing import Union\n\nasync def read_json(url: str) -> Union[dict, list]:\n    '''\n    Read a json file from a url safely\n    and return the parsed json object\n    '''\n    parsed = urlparse(url)\n    if parsed.scheme not in ('http', 'https'):\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid URL scheme. Only http and https are allowed.\")\n\n    async with httpx.AsyncClient() as client:\n        try:\n            response = await client.get(url, timeout=10.0)\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n        except httpx.HTTPError as e:\n            # Log error appropriately\n            raise ConnectionError(f\"Failed to fetch JSON: {e}\")"
